 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Types and gain grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The three types share every figure except voltage: BCP51 is rated -45 V collector-base and collector-emitter, BCP52 -60 V for both, BCP53 -100 V collector-base and -80 V collector-emitter. The suffix is the gain grade at IC = -150 mA: -10 for 63 to 160, -16 for 100 to 250. The full part number, for example BCP51-16, is the marking on the body."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = -2 V the gain is near 290 at 100 °C and near 200 at 25 °C from -1 mA to about -30 mA, then falls with rising current, to about 100 to 140 at -600 mA and about 30 to 60 at -1 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With base current one tenth of the collector current, VCE(sat) stays at about -23 to -32 mV below -10 mA and rises to about -340 mV at -25 °C and about -450 mV at 100 °C at -1 A (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about -350 mV (100 °C) and -540 mV (-25 °C) at -0.1 mA to about -910 and -950 mV at -1 A (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz the input capacitance Cib falls from about 110 pF at -0.1 V reverse bias to about 37 pF at -11 V, and the output capacitance Cob from about 41 pF at -0.1 V to about 8 pF at -29 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-223 body uses a molding compound rated UL 94V-0, is RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, with lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C."
  }
 ],
